# exercises the "no geometry at all" boundary. load_obj() itself still
# returns true (parsing succeeded), but state.objects stays empty since
# finalize_object() no-ops on parser_state_object_is_empty(); it's
# Application::load_obj_file() that then treats an empty object list as
# a hard failure ("no mesh objects found in ...").
#
# expected to be rejected at the Application layer -- run this one alone,
# not mixed into a multi-path invocation (Application::load_obj_paths
# bails out on the first failing path and never loads the rest).

